{
  "name": "Multi-location operators: operations and facilities leaders at regional chains",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Multi-location operators: operations and facilities leaders at regional chains\n\n### How it works\nChains buy once for many locations. Once a month Argorant counts directors and VPs of operations, facilities managers and regional or area managers at retail, restaurant, medical practice and fitness companies with 201 to 5,000 employees in your country, a good proxy for regional and multi-site operators. If the count is within max_people, the search is saved as a list, a campaign draft with two short emails is created, and the list joins the draft once it has filled; otherwise nothing is saved or spent. Slack gets the numbers either way.\n\nCosts: free until the list is added, then 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set country and max_people in **Settings**; change industries or sizes in the count node.\n4. Edit the emails in **Create the campaign draft**, pick the channel in **Report** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nSplit by industry into separate campaigns for sharper emails.",
        "height": 653,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "8ade80ab-651b-45dc-bdcf-35d676e12804",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Size\nFree count of operations leaders at mid-size chains, checked against max_people.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "67c035fd-9698-42fb-8d4a-f6b3df84ea96",
